{"sections":[],"metadata":{"title":"Tracking How a Screen Was Opened","role":"article","roleHeading":"Article","modules":[{"name":"ScreenStates"}]},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"seeAlsoSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenOpenSource"],"title":"Related Documentation","anchor":"Related-Documentation"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenOpenSource"],"title":"Navigation context","generated":true,"anchor":"Navigation-context"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates"]]},"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"Overview","text":"Overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenState","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" only model what a screen is showing right now — Empty, Loading, Data, or Error. They don’t know, and don’t need to know, how the screen got there. "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenOpenSource","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" is a separate, independent type for exactly that: was the screen freshly pushed, revealed by popping something off a navigation stack, presented modally, opened from a deep link, or launched from a Home Screen shortcut?"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"ScreenStates can’t detect any of this on its own — there’s no "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NavigationStack"},{"type":"text","text":" modifier or UIKit push interception behind "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenOpenSource","isActive":true},{"type